Attendance percentages are only as good as the calendar behind them. A holiday that isn't
configured is a day the whole school appears to have skipped.

## Working days

In **Administration → Settings**, set which days of the week your institute runs, then **Save
Working Days**. Everything else is calculated against this, so do it before term starts.

## The Calendar page

Holidays now live on **Administration → Calendar** (the old *Holidays* screen and *Events* screen
were merged into it; old links to Holidays open the Calendar's **Holidays** tab). It has two tabs:

- **Upcoming** — events and holidays still ahead, in date order.
- **Holidays** — every holiday and term break you have defined. These are the single source of truth
  for which days count as a school day, and drive attendance percentages and report cards everywhere.

A card at the top shows **School days held in** the current year: working days from 1 January up to
today, leaving out weekends, holidays and days outside term dates. If that number looks wrong, your
calendar is the reason.

Everyone with staff access can read the Calendar. Only administrators see the buttons to add, edit
or delete.

## Adding a holiday

1. Open **Administration → Calendar** and choose the **Holidays** tab.
2. Select **Add Holiday**.
3. Fill in:
   - **Title** — what it is called on reports. *Enter a title* is the error if it is empty.
   - **Date range** — pick the first and last day (two clicks; nothing is pre-selected). *Pick the
     first and last day* is the error if you have not.
   - **School holiday** or **Term break**. Term breaks bound the terms that
     [term attendance](/docs/educonnect-teacher-class-attendance) and progress reports are
     calculated over, so the distinction matters.
   - **Classes** — leave empty for all classes, or pick specific ones. This is how you record a
     year group being away on a trip without marking the whole school absent.
4. Select **Create**. You will see **Holiday created**.

The list shows each holiday with its dates, type, and **All classes** or the classes it applies to.
**Delete** asks first (*Delete holiday?*), and warns that it affects attendance percentages and
report cards. If it says *No holidays yet. Add one to get started.*, nothing is configured — and
every non-teaching day so far is being counted against your attendance figures.

## Closing the school today

If the school is unexpectedly shut, select **Mark today a holiday**. Enter a **Reason** (required —
*Enter a reason*), optionally choose classes (empty means every class), and select **Mark as
holiday**. Attendance percentages and reports skip the day, and you will see **Today marked as a
holiday**.

## Adding an event

On the **Upcoming** tab, **Add Event** takes a **Title**, optional **Details**, a date and an icon.
*Editing* an event changes that one occurrence. Recurring series are created from the dashboard
calendar rather than here.

## Terms

Term dates are set in **Administration → Settings** (and, for a school group, centrally in the head
office **Configuration → Term Dates**). Save them with **Save Terms**.

Get terms in before entering exam results: an exam sitting outside every configured term won't land
in the term it belongs to.

## Do this first

If attendance percentages look implausibly low, check this page before investigating anything else.
Unconfigured weekends, holidays and term breaks are by far the most common cause.

